<chapter xml:id="ch-season6" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Season 6: Equations</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> 
        An equation is a line of mathematics containing an = sign. 
        Equations communicate that the quantity on the left side of the = is equal to the quantity on the right side of the = sign.
      </p>
      <p>
        Equations can be used to express known facts (e.g. “I know that the value of A is 5, so <m>A=5</m>”). 
        Equations can also be used to expressed desired results (e.g. “I want the value of A to be 5, so <m>A = 5</m>”). 
      </p>
      <p>
       In this lesson, we will learn how to “solve” equations that contain a variable. 
       “Solving” an equation means finding the value of the variable that will make the equation true or which will achieve the desired result.  
      </p>
  </introduction>
